<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🍂 LIVE LEAF COLOR</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/leaf_color/legend.png?v=r13" width="600" alt="legend"><br>What each color means (one trip around the year, left to right on the key): <b>deep blue</b> = dormant winter; <b>light blue/cyan</b> = spring awakening and bud break; <b>teal-green</b> = leaf emergence; <b>green</b> = growing season; <b>yellow-green/yellow</b> = first color; <b>orange</b> = autumn coloring; <b>red/magenta</b> = peak color into leaf drop; <b>purple</b> = late drop returning to <b>deep-blue</b> dormant (the scale wraps: both ends are winter). Color is the satellite-derived growth stage, not the color of individual trees. Every vegetated land pixel is painted from the newest clear HLS observation in the rolling window; persistent gaps fall back to the most recent valid observation. <b>Transparent = cities, bare ground, open water, or non-vegetated land</b>.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NASA HLS v2.0 Landsat 8/9 + Sentinel-2 via Planetary Computer (30 m)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🍂 LIVE LEAF COLOR — auto-refresh</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/leaf_color/legend.png?v=r13" width="600" alt="legend"><br>What each color means (one trip around the year, left to right on the key): <b>deep blue</b> = dormant winter; <b>light blue/cyan</b> = spring awakening and bud break; <b>teal-green</b> = leaf emergence; <b>green</b> = growing season; <b>yellow-green/yellow</b> = first color; <b>orange</b> = autumn coloring; <b>red/magenta</b> = peak color into leaf drop; <b>purple</b> = late drop returning to <b>deep-blue</b> dormant (the scale wraps: both ends are winter). Color is the satellite-derived growth stage, not the color of individual trees. Every vegetated land pixel is painted from the newest clear HLS observation in the rolling window; persistent gaps fall back to the most recent valid observation. <b>Transparent = cities, bare ground, open water, or non-vegetated land</b>.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NASA HLS v2.0 Landsat 8/9 + Sentinel-2 via Planetary Computer (30 m)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Leaf_Color.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>604800</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
